    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add a federated identity guide]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41779</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41779"/>
        <updated>2025-11-05T03:11:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">This PR adds a guide to federated identity.</p>
<p dir="auto">It's not finished yet, but it's definitely ready for some review.</p>
<p dir="auto">What's done</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>an overview of what it is</li>
<li>a moderately close look at the main flow in OpenID Connect</li>
<li>a short but sufficient (I think) discussion of the use of third-party cookies in federated identity systems</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">What's not done:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>a section on using specific identity providers. I want to say, people adding support for federated identity will always need to choose a provider, and providers will greatly reduce the amount of complexity they need to deal with. I think it is most helpful to name specific providers, such as Google and GitHub and (in a slightly different way I suppose) Auth0 but I don't like the idea of seeming to pick winners or entrench monopolies.</li>
<li>a section introducing FedCM. I want especially to talk about:
<ul dir="auto">
<li>how this fixes third-party cookie issues, greatly simplifies the work the RP needs to do, and promises a better and more consistent UX</li>
<li>how it's not cross-browser yet (and thus can't really be recommended yet) but that we're hopeful it will become so.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>probably something tying it together, which should describe some of the limitations of fed ID (especially, about it excluding people who don't want to or can't sign up with your chosen IdP).</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Note that preview images are broken because of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3510366053" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/904" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/fred/issues/904/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/904">mdn/fred#904</a>.</strong></p>]]></content>
